  "description": [
    {
      "value": "<p>A cut board that sets the level at which one terrace basin spills into the next, notched along its upper edge in eleven steps and dropped into slots in the retaining wall. The notches are not equal: they follow the stages of what is being grown or settled in the basin above, so the board encodes a schedule as well as a height. It is water-stained to different depths at four of the eleven steps, which are the four in ordinary use. Recovered from a collapsed section of wall, sound, and still fitting the slots either side of it.</p>",
      "inLanguage": [{ "id": ["core.peerdb.org", "LANGUAGE", "en-GB"] }]
    }
